      "content": "but it doesn't feel like i can just \"make it right.\" every time i see them smiling, i just think about how much they expect of me and how much i've already let them down. it's like this constant weight in my chest. i feel like if i just wasn't here, the shame wouldn't be there anymore. they wouldn't have to deal with the embarrassment of a kid who couldn't make it.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
